      "lineAnnotations": {
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: prints the character in A through the current channel (CURCHL), by PRINT_A_CHAN.","comment":"PRINT_A_CHAN"},
        "19": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "20": {"comment":"$15 here ($FF in the 48K ROM), never run"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"The keyboard part of INT_FRAME: INT_KBD_MOTOR (the keyboard, then in +3 BASIC the disk\nmotor's time-out) with BC and DE kept, then the registers back and EI."},
        "74": {"comment":"The keyboard, then the motor (INT_KBD_MOTOR)"},
        "79": {"comment":"HL and AF back"},
        "81": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: when NMIADD ($5CB0) is not zero it jumps there (JP (HL)); when it is zero\nit returns at once (NMI_RETURN). The 48K ROM's test is the other way round.","comment":"AF and HL kept"},
        "104": {"comment":"HL = NMIADD"},
        "107": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "109": {"comment":"Zero: just return"},
        "111": {"comment":"To NMIADD"},
        "2416": {"synopsis":"SAVE: \"Press REC & PLAY, then any key.\" in the lower screen (TAPE_MESSAGES), a key\n(WAIT_KEY), the header (17 bytes, flag 0, SA_BYTES), a gap of 50 interrupts, then the data\n(flag $FF)."},
        "2422": {"comment":"Message 0: \"Press REC & PLAY, then any key.\""},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"Tape messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE (read from $0977): entry 0 is empty ($80); then \"Press REC\n& PLAY, then any key.\", and, each after a $0D, \"Program: \", \"Number array: \", \"Character\narray: \" and \"Bytes: \".\nObserved: SAVE \"x\" in 48 BASIC printed \"Press REC & PLAY, then any key.\""},
        "2496": {"synopsis":"Read as a table from here (LOAD_HEADER_SHOW, DE = $09C0): entry 0 is the last byte of \"Press\nREC & PLAY, then any key.\", entries 1-4 the kinds of file, so type n prints entry n + 1."},
        "2898": {"synopsis":"$90 and up: first OUT_NEW_TOKENS, for $A3 and $A4 (SPECTRUM and PLAY in +3 BASIC); then as\nin the 48K ROM: $90-$A4 the UDG A - $90, from UDG (OUT_CHAR_BC), $A5 and up OUT_TOKEN.","comment":"$A3/$A4 first (OUT_NEW_TOKENS)"},
        "2901": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"Prints the report's code character (PRINT_A_DIGIT), a space, then its message; then\nHOOK_REPORT, which in this version always does what it replaced (no hook into the other\nROM).","comment":"Printed"},
        "4927": {"comment":"A space"},
        "4930": {"comment":"A = the number"},
        "4931": {"comment":"The message for the number, from REPORT_MESSAGES"},
        "4937": {"comment":"Message 0, DE = COMMA_MESSAGES (HOOK_REPORT)"},
        "4940": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "4944": {"comment":"The line number, PPC ($FFFE for a direct command prints as 0)"},
        "4951": {"comment":"':'"},
        "4954": {"comment":"The statement number, SUBPPC"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4962": {"comment":"Empty the edit line, keeping its $0D"},
        "4965": {"comment":"Report 0: no CONTINUE position"},
        "4971": {"comment":"Reports 9 (STOP statement) and L (BREAK into program) continue after the statement"},
        "4975": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "5432": {"synopsis":"Start-up messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE: entry 0 is a lone space, entry 1 the copyright line\n(the $7F character, \" 1982 Amstrad\" and 14 spaces, the last with bit 7 set), which start-up\nprints as message 0.\nObserved: 48 BASIC started with the $7F character and \" 1982 Amstrad\"."},
        "7037": {"synopsis":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)? Through HOOK_STMT_JUMP, which in this version always\ntests it here.","comment":"A jump pending? (HOOK_STMT_JUMP)"},
        "7040": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instruction"},
        "7041": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "7043": {"comment":"HL = NEWPPC"},
        "7046": {"comment":"Bit 15: the edit line?"},
        "7048": {"comment":"No: a program line"},
        "7156": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C. The test goes through HOOK_STMT_NEXT, which in this version always does it\nhere.","comment":"The current character, ENTER? (HOOK_STMT_NEXT)"},
        "7161": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7166": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "9780": {"synopsis":"INKEY$: with '#' a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX, operation $1A). Otherwise, when\nrunning, the key held now as a one-character string, or an empty one (INKEY_KEYS: the\nkeyboard).","comment":"Priority 16, operation $5A"},
        "9783": {"comment":"Past INKEY$"},
        "9784": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "9786": {"comment":"Then a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX)"},
        "9789": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9792": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9794": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9796": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9798": {"comment":"The key held (INKEY_KEYS)"},
        "9801": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Too many keys: empty"},
        "9805": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "9808": {"comment":"No key: empty"},
        "9810": {"comment":"D = $FF: bit 3 set, L mode"},
        "9811": {"comment":"E = the main code"},
        "9812": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE, MODE 0)"},
        "14446": {"synopsis":"The frame interrupt's keys and disk motor: the keyboard (KEYBOARD), then in +3 BASIC (FLAGS\nbit 4 set) the motor's time-out (MOTOR_TIMEOUT). Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "14448": {"comment":"The keyboard (KEYBOARD)"},
        "14451": {"comment":"+3 BASIC?"},
        "14457": {"comment":"The motor's time-out (MOTOR_TIMEOUT)"},
        "14460": {"synopsis":"IX back."},
        "14463": {"synopsis":"Counts the disk motor's time-out down: with bank 7 paged in (the paging byte $5B5C with bits\n0-2 set, to port $7FFD), when the count at $E600 is not 0 and FRAMES is even, the count goes\ndown by one; when it reaches 0, bit 3 of port $1FFD is cleared (its copy at $5B67 too),\nwhich turns the motor off. Then port $7FFD gets $5B5C back.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nObserved: in +3 BASIC, with $E600 set to 6 and bit 3 of $5B67 set, the count reached 0 within\n20 frames and bit 3 was cleared (ROM 0 may count too, so the rate is not this routine's).","comment":"Bank 7 paged in"},
        "14473": {"comment":"The count at $E600 (bank 7)"},
        "14476": {"comment":"0: nothing to do"},
        "14479": {"comment":"FRAMES' low byte"},
        "14482": {"comment":"An odd frame: wait"},
        "14486": {"comment":"One less"},
        "14493": {"comment":"Not yet 0"},
        "14495": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "14498": {"comment":"Its copy, bit 3 (the motor) cleared"},
        "14508": {"synopsis":"Port $7FFD gets the paging byte $5B5C back.","comment":"The paging byte back"},
        "14517": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $39FF."},
        "14848": {"synopsis":"HL = $3D03, then ROM_SWAP_HL. Nothing in this ROM calls it, so it is entered from another\nROM."},
        "14853": {"synopsis":"HL = $3D06, then ROM_SWAP_HL. Nothing in this ROM calls it either."},
        "14856": {"synopsis":"Leaves this ROM for another with HL as its argument: A kept in AF', the copy of port $1FFD\n($5B67) pushed, then stored and written with bit 2 cleared, interrupts off. Bit 2 of port\n$1FFD is the high bit of the ROM number, so ROM 3 (this one) gives way to ROM 1, and the\njump to $3D00 runs there. ROM_SWAP_BACK is the way back.","comment":"A kept"},
        "14857": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "14860": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "14863": {"comment":"Kept for the way back"},
        "14864": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared: the ROM below"},
        "14872": {"comment":"To $3D00 in the ROM now paged in"},
        "14875": {"synopsis":"The way back into this ROM: A kept in AF', the copy of port $1FFD saved by ROM_SWAP_HL\npopped, stored and written with interrupts off, then interrupts on and A back. Execution\ncomes here because the other ROM pages this one back in.","comment":"A kept"},
        "14876": {"comment":"The copy saved by ROM_SWAP_HL"},
        "14881": {"comment":"Stored, then written"},
        "14889": {"synopsis":"REPORT_CHAR's hook: FLAGS bit 4 tested, but the jump that would follow it is two NOPs, so it\nalways does what it replaced: A = 0 and DE = COMMA_MESSAGES.","comment":"+3 BASIC? (not acted on)"},
        "14893": {"comment":"Where the jump to HOOK_TO_010F would be"},
        "14895": {"comment":"A = 0, DE = COMMA_MESSAGES"},
        "14900": {"synopsis":"HL = $010F, then ROM0_JUMP. Nothing comes here in this version."},
        "14903": {"synopsis":"Continues at address HL in the other ROM: HL goes on the stack in place of the return\naddress (which is left in HL), and the routine at $5B00 in RAM swaps the ROMs and returns\nthere.","comment":"HL to the stack, the return address to HL"},
        "14907": {"synopsis":"STMT_JUMP's hook: FLAGS bit 4 tested with the jump after it NOPped out, so always what it\nreplaced: NSPPC bit 7 tested (Z: a jump pending).","comment":"+3 BASIC? (not acted on)"},
        "14913": {"comment":"A jump pending?"},
        "14918": {"synopsis":"HL = $0112, then ROM0_JUMP. Nothing comes here in this version."},
        "14923": {"synopsis":"STMT_NEXT's hook: FLAGS bit 4 tested with the jump after it NOPped out, so always what it\nreplaced: the current character compared with ENTER.","comment":"+3 BASIC? (not acted on)"},
        "14929": {"comment":"The current character, ENTER?"},
        "14933": {"synopsis":"HL = $0115, then ROM0_JUMP. Nothing comes here in this version."},
        "14938": {"synopsis":"INKEY$'s key: the keyboard as in the 48K ROM (READ_KEYS, KEY_MAIN_CODE, KEY_DECODE). A key\ngoes to OP_INKEY_CHAR, none to INKEY_NO_KEY.","comment":"The keys held (READ_KEYS)"},
        "14941": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "14943": {"comment":"Too many keys"},
        "14945": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "14948": {"comment":"No key"},
        "14950": {"comment":"D = $FF: L mode"},
        "14952": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE)"},
        "14955": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "14958": {"synopsis":"No key: an empty string (OP_INKEY_STR). In +3 BASIC it goes through DI, EI and a jump to the\nnext instruction first, where ROM 1 of the 128K reads its keypad.","comment":"+3 BASIC?"},
        "14962": {"comment":"48 BASIC: empty"},
        "14965": {"comment":"In place of the keypad"},
        "14969": {"synopsis":"No key: an empty string.","comment":"C = 0"},
        "14974": {"synopsis":"OUT_UDG_TOKEN's first step: codes $A3 and $A4 in +3 BASIC print SPECTRUM and PLAY\n(NEW_TOKEN_NAMES) through PRINT_TOKEN's printing, spaced as a keyword; anything else, and\n$A3/$A4 in 48 BASIC (where they are UDGs), goes on as in the 48K ROM: OUT_TOKEN from $A5,\nOUT_UDG below.","comment":"SPECTRUM?"},
        "14978": {"comment":"PLAY?"},
        "14982": {"synopsis":"As in the 48K ROM: a keyword from $A5 (OUT_TOKEN), a UDG below (OUT_UDG)."},
        "14990": {"synopsis":"$A3 or $A4: a keyword in +3 BASIC only.","comment":"+3 BASIC?"},
        "14996": {"comment":"Return to NEW_KEYWORD_END"},
        "15002": {"comment":"DE = SPECTRUM"},
        "15007": {"comment":"Or PLAY"},
        "15010": {"synopsis":"Printed with the token rule's spaces (4 on the stack: a space after), from PRINT_ENTRY's\ntest of FIND_ENTRY's carry (PRINT_ENTRY_AT)."},
        "15016": {"synopsis":"After it: on the printer (FLAGS bit 1) done; on the screen the position fetched again\n(FETCH_POS)."},
        "15025": {"synopsis":"The names of keywords $A3 and $A4 in +3 BASIC, last letter with bit 7 set: SPECTRUM, PLAY."},
        "15037": {"synopsis":"Jumps to $3C01, where this ROM has text bytes, not code (TEST_TEXT). Nothing comes here."},
        "15040": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3BE0."},
        "15329": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3BFE."},
        "15359": {"synopsis":"Two bytes of $FF."},
        "15361": {"synopsis":"Text bytes with no routine here to print them: BRIGHT 0, \"19\", BRIGHT 1, \"87\"."},
        "15369": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3C96."},
        "15511": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to the character set."}
      }
    }
  },
